<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.huffmanwrites.daily-sitrep</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/bin/bash</string>
    <string>/Users/prh/Developer/huffmanwrites/scripts/daily-sitrep-runner.sh</string>
  </array>
  <!-- Every day at 06:00 CT. Philip asked for a report every day of the week
       (2026-10-07); the shape he chose from the options put to him was a single
       daily Global SITREP rather than a new weekly series for each empty
       weekday, and the beats he chose were the courts, the administration and
       the rule of law, markets and the economy, and elections and civics. AI and
       technology was a fifth beat and was removed on 2026-10-07; the pack does
       not read those tags and the writer must not carry the subject.

       A single dict with Hour and Minute and no Weekday key fires daily, which
       is exactly the requirement here and is why the shape is one dict: the
       schedule says "once a day, every day" and nothing else. (An ARRAY of
       dicts also works in a LaunchAgent — com.huffmanwrites.docket-watch has
       used that form since 2026-09-20 and fires at both of its times daily. An
       older comment here claimed launchd ignores an array; that was wrong, and
       what actually went wrong in the case it was written for was a double
       hyphen inside an XML comment, which is what check-plists.py names.)

       06:00 rather than 07:00 because 07:00 already holds two jobs (weekly
       satire on Mondays, the Senate race report on Sundays), 08:00 holds the
       docket report on Saturdays, and 13:00 through 14:00 on Mondays holds
       site-audit, wiki-check and weekly-integrity. A daily job cannot afford to
       be the one that collides.

       This job does NOT replace any of them. It is the daily edition; the
       weekly series keep their own days and their own beats. -->
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Hour</key>
    <integer>6</integer>
    <key>Minute</key>
    <integer>0</integer>
  </dict>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>/Users/prh/Developer/huffmanwrites</string>
  <!-- Keep the exported PATH used by the other huffmanwrites jobs so claude,
       hugo, python3 and the keychain-backed helpers resolve the same way. -->
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/Users/prh/.local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
    <key>HOME</key>
    <string>/Users/prh</string>
  </dict>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/prh/Library/Logs/daily-sitrep.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/prh/Library/Logs/daily-sitrep.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
